# Rust
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# WebAssembly build output (wasm-pack / wasm-bindgen / trunk)
/pkg/
**/pkg/
*.wasm

# Web frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vitest browser-mode artifacts. Written only when a browser test FAILS, so they are absent on a
# green tree and would otherwise be committed by whoever happens to run the suite after a red one.
.vitest-attachments/
**/__screenshots__/

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs, editor, OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/

# Agent worktrees
/.claude/worktrees/

# Repo-local dev tooling scripts/setup-dev.sh installs (e.g. the pinned tree-sitter CLI), so a
# developer's machine matches what CI runs without polluting $PATH or a system directory.
/.tools/

# Playwright MCP session output — screenshots and page snapshots from browser-driving tools.
# Never source; regenerated on demand and easily swept in by `git add -A`.
.playwright-mcp/
# ...and stray screenshots a browser tool wrote to a relative path outside it.
redextape-*.png

# `tree-sitter build -o parser.so` writes here, and it is an EDITOR that runs it rather than anything
# in this repository: nvim-treesitter's local-path install compiles in place, inside whichever
# checkout it was pointed at. `plugin/redextape.lua` points it at this one, so a developer who
# installs the grammars through Neovim gets four untracked binaries in a tree that was clean before.
# Not swept up by `/target/` above — these sit beside the committed `src/parser.c`, not under it.
grammars/*/parser.so
